      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand your need for more concrete indicators. Here are some additional questions and scenarios focusing on impulsivity, deference to authority, and linguistic styles:\n\n1. Impulsivity:\n   - \"Think of a time when you made a quick decision without thinking it through. How do you typically react to instantaneous situations? Can you share an experience where acting impulsively led to a significant consequence?\"\n   - \"How do you handle waiting in lines or doing tedious tasks? Do you prefer to get a task done quickly and constantly seek quicker solutions, even if they aren't the best?\"\n\n2. Deference to Authority:\n   - \"Describe a time when someone in authority made a change that didn't feel fair to you. How did you respond and why? What values are important to you in a leader or authority figure?\"\n   - \"If you disagree with someone in a position of authority, how do you express your disagreement? Do you strive for mediation, confrontation, compliance, or avoidance?\"\n\n3. Linguistic Styles:\n   - \"How often do you use slang or colloquial language? Does the type of language you use change in different environments (e.g., with family vs. friends)? Can you give an example of how a particular situation or group might",
